<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Standard Galactic Suite (SGS)</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} is a monorepo of fifteen interdisciplinary software prototypes unified under a formal theory of </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">entropy-aware computation</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}. This essay presents a rigorous mathematical framework wherein polyglot modularity, recursive semantics, and automated epistemology are modeled as dynamical systems over information-theoretic manifolds. We introduce the </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Recursive Semantic Vector Plenum (RSVP)</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} as a core dynamical system, prove coherence convergence, and demonstrate its instantiation across linguistic, physical, and interactive domains. The CI/CD pipeline is formalized as a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">hermeneutic feedback loop</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}, and the dashboard system as a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">low-entropy epistemic mirror</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">abstract</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
