<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Standard Galactic Suite (SGS)</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} constitutes a monorepo comprising fifteen interdisciplinary prototypes unified under a comprehensive theory of </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">entropy-aware polyglot computation</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}. This extended treatise establishes a fully rigorous mathematical framework wherein recursive semantics, sheaf-theoretic modularity, dynamical epistemology, and information-theoretic ethics are formalized as interconnected dynamical systems over differentiable manifolds equipped with Riemannian metrics derived from relative entropy. We introduce the </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Recursive Semantic Vector Plenum (RSVP)</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} as a second-order stochastic differential system, prove </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">strong coherence convergence</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} under Lyapunov stability, and instantiate it across symbolic, physical, and interactive domains with explicit error bounds. The CI/CD pipeline is modeled as a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">contractive hermeneutic operator</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} on the space of repository states, with convergence rates quantified via spectral gap analysis. The dashboard emerges as a </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">low-entropy epistemic mirror</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} inducing a global section in the polyglot sheaf. Human--computer interaction is framed via </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">variational free energy minimization</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}, with empirical validation through Gaussian process regression on user telemetry. We conclude with open conjectures on computational cosmology and entropy ethics.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">abstract</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
