<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\section</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{Introduction and Foundational Axioms}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Standard Galactic Suite</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} transcends conventional software engineering paradigms by positing computation as an </span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">epistemic process</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} governed by entropy minimization across heterogeneous domains. Its fifteen projectsâ€”ranging from symbolic algebra (SGA, </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\lambda</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">-Arabic) to physical simulation (Crystal Plenum) and interactive systems (Agora Pacer, Swype Hero)â€”are unified by the following axiomatic structure:</span></span>
